---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const DISCORD = 'https://discord.gg/p9Xc45txWa';
---

<Layout
  path="/hosting"
  title="Hosted nests - Nuthatch"
  description="Send a contract and a chain; we build the nest, keep it at the chain's tip on our servers and hand you an endpoint. Free, with no billing and no accounts."
>
  <section class="page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="section-label">Hosting</p>
      <h1>We host your nest. You get an endpoint.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Rather not run the binary yourself? Send us a contract and its chain. We build the nest, check it against
        the chain, and keep it at the tip on our own servers. You get a URL with SQL and HTTP over the contract's
        whole history, and help when something does not answer the way you expected. Free, with no billing and no
        accounts.
      </p>

      <p class="ask">
        Ask on the <a href={DISCORD} rel="noopener">Nuthatch Discord</a>, or in a GitHub issue that mentions
        nuthatch. A nest over a few contracts is usually up the same day.
      </p>

      <div class="notes">
        <section>
          <h2>What to send</h2>
          <p>
            The contract addresses and the chain, and the start block if you know it. If a contract is not verified,
            send its ABI. A line on what your app asks of it helps us check the answers it will need.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>What you get</h2>
          <p>
            An endpoint serving <code>/sql</code>, entity reads over HTTP and <code>/ready</code>, which says how far
            it has indexed. It follows the tip and handles reorgs, on any EVM chain with a JSON-RPC endpoint. The RPC
            is ours to pay for.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>Take it home any time</h2>
          <p>
            A hosted nest is the stock binary run as any operator would run it. You get its config and its identity,
            and the same nest run on your machine seals the same bytes. Leaving costs you nothing.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <section class="kinds">
        <h2>What we host</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Contract nests.</strong> A contract's events, factories and the pools or vaults they create, with
          SQL views over them. The <a href="/nests#hosted">public ones are listed on Nests</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Account history.</strong> An Etherscan-shaped <code>/api</code> for chains whose explorer API is
          paid or gone, for rotki and anything else that speaks it. A hosted one sees the addresses you ask about;
          if that matters, <a href="https://github.com/nuthatch-org/nuthatch/tree/main/examples/paywalled-chains" rel="noopener">run it yourself</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Subgraph ports.</strong> A subgraph The Graph no longer serves, ported to a nest from the same
          contracts. <a href="/subgraphs">Nest-backed subgraphs</a> says what answers exactly and what is refused.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="kinds">
        <h2>The terms</h2>
        <p>
          It runs on our own boxes, kept up the way we keep our own nests up, with no SLA. If you need one, the same
          nest runs on yours. There is no account, no key and no quota, so there is nothing to sign up for and nothing
          to cancel.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem) clamp(4rem, 9vw, 6.5rem); }
  h1 { margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
  .lede { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 2.2rem; max-width: 64ch; }
  .ask {
    border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.2rem 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.75rem; margin: 0;
  }
  .notes { margin-top: 3rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(18rem, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 2rem; }
  .notes h2 { font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .notes p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0; }
  .kinds { margin-top: 2.5rem; max-width: 64ch; }
  .kinds h2 { font-size: 1.125rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .kinds p { color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 0.8rem; }
  .kinds strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
</style>
